.TH LIBMPQ__WRITER_BEGIN 3 2026-08-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__writer_begin \- begin an MPQ streaming file writer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__writer_begin("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "mpq_archive,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t " "unpacked_size,"
.BI "        const mpq_file_options_s *" "options,"
.BI "        mpq_writer_s **" "writer"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Begins \fIfilename\fP with declared \fIunpacked_size\fP and returns an
active, caller-owned \fI*writer\fP. The member filename must be nonempty.
A declared size of zero is valid. NULL \fIoptions\fP selects writer
defaults. Supply bytes with libmpq__writer_write(3), then call
libmpq__writer_finish(3). Only one writer may be active per archive. The archive
must outlive the writer. Closing the archive with an active writer reports an
error and discards that writer; neither handle may then be reused.
.PP
Ordinary writes accept LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_IMPLODE, LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_COMPRESS,
LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_ENCRYPTED, LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_KEY, LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_SINGLE and
LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_SECTOR_CRC. Unsupported bits, including PATCH_FILE and
DELETE_MARKER, return LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT. IMPLODE and COMPRESS are mutually
exclusive. KEY without ENCRYPTED has no encryption effect. Existing codec
restrictions apply.
.PP
Add LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_SECTOR_CRC to options.flags to generate sector Adler-32
checksums for sectorized COMPRESS or IMPLODE files. Checksums cover packed
bytes before encryption. The checksum table follows the data and is not
encrypted; it uses zlib compression only when smaller than raw storage.
The flag is ignored for empty, raw, and single-unit files. Generation is
opt-in and does not enable implicit verification during extraction.
.PP
SINGLE storage is independent of the archive sector size. A newly oversized
unit buffers its complete declared input, is encoded/encrypted once, and remains
one logical block without a sector-offset or sector-CRC table. The new path is
limited to min(INT32_MAX, UINT32_MAX, SIZE_MAX) by current representation and
one-block reader transfer types, with additional codec and output-extent checks.
Existing inputs fitting a configured sector retain their prior behavior.
Encoding may require several times the input size in memory. There is no fixed
MiB cap or library-managed memory budget. Applications handling untrusted sizes
should apply their own resource limits. Normal allocation failures are reported
where the runtime returns control; this does not guarantee survival of OOM
termination. Existing codec/version restrictions and ADPCM SINGLE rejection,
KEY adjustments, generated listfile defaults and physical patch defaults remain.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fB0\fP with an active writer on success, or a
negative libmpq error. No file entry is published before finish succeeds.
.SH ERRORS
Invalid writer state or storage options return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT\fP;
NULL, empty or duplicate filenames return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP.
Invalid sizes or exhausted capacity return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE\fP.
Allocation and I/O errors may also propagate.
